    <<link "Refuse<br>">>
    <<replace"#choice">>
        Finally understanding that he asked if you wanted to join him, you politely decline. Whether you have something else to do, are not one for sweets, or just feel this hyperactive little boy is too much for you to handle. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Luca</span>’s expression falls for a second, but it quickly returns. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“No worries, more candy for me then!”</span> He laughs, <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“I’ll tell you all about it. Maybe find out the best one so you can try-”</span> You worry he is going to go off on a long, hyperactive ramble again when the store suddenly opens and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Luca</span> sprints inside with excitement, nearly knocking over the teenage cashier that opened the store. <br>
        <br>
        You’re pretty sure the kid should lay off the sugar a little, though he is very cute when he’s this hyper. <br>
